  "title": "Daemon: never dispatch, gate or merge a goal-container task (constraints.goal true); goals close only via the closable decision when every execute child is merged",
  "spec": "Facts (Planner grep, provenance repo): daemon.stale(t) (daemon.py ~384-394) returns False for a parentless queued execute task, so a GOAL task (role execute, parent None, constraints.goal True, budget_turns 0, read_only True) is eligible for dispatch(); on 2026-09-23 08:49 the daemon dispatched T-0985 to Codex (sol, 324 s), the result posted done and closed the goal, and stale() then skipped gating its child T-0986. planner_runs.decision_points() already emits \"closable\" only when every execute child has merged_into (planner_runs.py ~206), and _condition_resolved treats the goal's status done as resolution. Goal tasks are created by the Planner with constraints goal true, read_only true, budget_turns 0.\nDo:\n1. daemon.py: a helper is_goal(t) = bool((t.get(\"constraints\") or {}).get(\"goal\")); dispatch(), gate(), the merge stage, auto_fix_round and reconcile_dead skip goal tasks entirely (containers, never work items); stale(t) returns True for any goal task so no stage touches it, while keeping today's behaviour for real tasks; a goal task that somehow carries dispatched_at is left alone and one notify line per daemon process says the goal task is a container.\n2. Goal closing: the only automatic path that may set a goal task to done is the closable decision in planner_runs (every execute child merged_into set, nothing queued or running). executor.start refuses to start a goal task with status refused and reason \"goal container\"; the worker result paths (spawn.run_worker result handling, executor.start/reply) refuse to post a result onto a goal task the same way; the Planner's own bus.post_result stays allowed.\n3. Tests (unittest, import _harness first): tests/test_daemon.py::test_goal_task_is_never_dispatched (a parentless queued execute task with constraints.goal true is not dispatched after a tick, while a child under it is), ::test_goal_task_is_skipped_by_gate_and_merge, ::test_goal_child_is_gated_while_goal_is_queued (a done child of a queued goal gets gated); tests/test_executor.py::test_start_refuses_goal_container; tests/test_planner_runs.py::test_closable_requires_every_execute_child_merged.\n4. docs/orchestrator-goals.md (new, at most 40 lines): goal containers, why they are never dispatched, how they close, the revert path (git revert). Never quote double-brace placeholder tokens literally. Do not ask questions; decide and note decisions in the result.",
